275	   * Runs the shutdown sequence, at most once per cycle. Callers that arrive
276	   * while a shutdown is already in flight - a process signal delivered during
277	   * an explicit `close()`, or the other way round - await the very same
278	   * promise instead of starting a second, concurrent teardown.
